# Nuxeo API Patterns

Before adding a new API call, check AGENTS/01-services.md — the method may already exist.
If it does not exist, add it to the appropriate service file.

## Always inject NuxeoApiBase — never HttpClient directly

```typescript
@Injectable({ providedIn: 'root' })
export class MyDomainService {
  private readonly api = inject(NuxeoApiBase);  // correct
  // private readonly http = inject(HttpClient); // NEVER in services
}
```

## Standard GET

```typescript
getDocument(uid: string): Observable<NuxeoDocument> {
  return this.api.get<NuxeoDocument>(`/nuxeo/api/v1/id/${uid}`);
}
```

## GET with enrichers

```typescript
getDocumentWithThumbnail(uid: string): Observable<NuxeoDocument> {
  return this.api.get<NuxeoDocument>(`/nuxeo/api/v1/id/${uid}`, {
    headers: { 'enrichers-document': 'thumbnail,permissions' }
  });
}
```

## Automation operation

```typescript
createCollection(title: string, description = ''): Observable<NuxeoDocument> {
  return this.api.post<NuxeoDocument>('/nuxeo/api/v1/automation/Collection.Create', {
    params: { name: title, description },
    context: {},
  });
}
```

## File upload (multipart)

```typescript
uploadFile(batchId: string, index: number, file: File): Observable<void> {
  const form = new FormData();
  form.append('file', file);
  return this.api.post<void>(`/nuxeo/api/v1/upload/${batchId}/${index}`, form);
}
```

## NEVER

- Never call HttpClient directly from a feature component
- Never hardcode `/nuxeo/api/v1` URLs in components — use services
- Never use `.snapshot` for route params in reusable components
- Never use the native `fetch()` API for Nuxeo calls (bypasses auth interceptor)
- Never add Authorization headers manually — the interceptor handles this

## After adding a new method

1. Export from `libs/shared/nuxeo-client/src/index.ts` if needed
2. Update `docs/api-integrations.md` with the new endpoint
3. Update `AGENTS/01-services.md` with the new method signature
4. Write a unit test in the same folder
